WEBVTT

00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:34.520
Our next challenge 
was to find such a path

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:38.470
that would take the Mars orbiter 
from Earth to Mars.

00:04:38.470 --> 00:04:42.890
If there were to be even a 0.1 percent 
difference from the predefined path,

00:04:42.890 --> 00:04:45.700
the orbiter would never 
be able to reach that planet.

00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:46.730
After 10 months,

00:04:46.730 --> 00:04:51.350
after having travelled a distance
of over 650 million kilometers,

00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:54.730
the Orbiter reached very close to Mars.

00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:56.750
Barely 500 kilometers left.

00:04:56.750 --> 00:05:00.330
But this didn’t mean 
that the mission was successful.